PARTITION BY department restarts the counter for each department. No two rows share the same number within a group.


RANK() vs DENSE_RANK()
Both handle ties, but differently:

RANK() — skips numbers after a tie (1, 1, 3…)
DENSE_RANK() — no gaps after a tie (1, 1, 2…)

sqlSELECT name, salary,
  RANK()       OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS rnk,
  DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS dense_rnk
FROM employees;
