NTILE(n)
Splits rows into n equal buckets and assigns a bucket number.
sqlSELECT name, salary,
  NTILE(3) OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS bucket
FROM employees;
-- Bucket 1 = top earners, Bucket 3 = bottom earners

2. Offset / navigation functions
These look at other rows relative to the current one.
LAG() and LEAD()

LAG(col, n) — value from n rows before the current row
LEAD(col, n) — value from n rows after the current row

sqlSELECT name, hire_date,
  LAG(name)  OVER (ORDER BY hire_date) AS prev_hired,
  LEAD(name) OVER (ORDER BY hire_date) AS next_hired
FROM employees;
