4. Running / cumulative calculations
Use ROWS BETWEEN to control the frame:
sqlSELECT name, hire_date, salary,
  SUM(salary) OVER (ORDER BY hire_date
                    ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) AS running_total
FROM employees;
This produces a running total — each row's value is salary added to all salaries of employees hired before them.

5. Distribution functions
PERCENT_RANK()
Returns the relative rank as a 0 to 1 percentage.
sqlSELECT name, salary,
  PERCENT_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY salary) AS pct_rank
FROM employees;
-- Formula: (rank - 1) / (total_rows - 1)
CUME_DIST()
Returns what fraction of rows have a value ≤ the current row's value.
sqlSELECT name, salary,
  CUME_DIST() OVER (ORDER BY salary) AS cumulative_dist
FROM employees;
-- Example: 0.71 means 71% of employees earn ≤ this salary

